## 6. Bed screw adjustment

The basic `SCREWS_TILT_CALCULATE` function is also available directly through the `Tools` section in Fluidd.

The `SCREWS_TILT` macro is a fully prepared version of the `SCREWS_TILT_CALCULATE` function. It homes the printer, heats the bed, heats the nozzle, and wipes the nozzle before starting. This helps ensure no filament is sticking out from the nozzle, which is important because the nozzle is also the bed probe.

The `Z_TILT` macro does a similar job, but includes homing, heating, and wiping for a smoother and more complete user experience than the stock function.

### Upgrade
Replacing the bed adjustment nuts and thumb nuts with nylock nuts and plain washers on each bed adjustment bolt makes bed tramming much easier.

I also replaced the original bed springs with much stronger springs: Blue 16 OD x 8.5 ID x 15 mm. These provide far more resistance when adjusting the bed.

